  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Employability of Host and Refugee Youth in Beirut</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project serves as a continuation to a recently completed one that received DSO funding (Improving Prospects for Refugees and Vulnerable Host Communities). It intends on making results more sustainable by focusing on the capacitation of the local partner to address the needs of the most vulnerable youth (15-24) living in urban areas of greater Beirut. Targeted youth are exposed to multiple forms of deprivation, exploitation and violence. Alternative livelihoods opportunities will be provided. Life skills, digital literacy, and English language are first provided, followed by a shift to vocational training or en trepreneurship. Either track is provided alongside digital upskilling sessions. Throughout the intervention, livelihoods counselling will be provided to support youth with making appropriate educational, training and occupational decisions. Nabad, the implementing local partner, will receive needs-based organizational and technical capacity building to continue operating two community centres where trainings for youth will be conducted. It is expected that they will be able to sustainably run these centers by the end of the project.</narrative>
  </description>
